{"duration_api_ms":92247,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"de6ccc93-fde4-4f58-82c8-6067c4a0f50c","total_cost_usd":0.41256919999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":66617,"cache_read_input_tokens":69201,"output_tokens":9210,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2476},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":66617,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3308,"cache_read_input_tokens":64879,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6060},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":40078,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.040153,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":9210,"cacheReadInputTokens":69201,"cacheCreationInputTokens":66617,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3724162,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2476,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1-topology\",\"requirement\":\"PostgreSQL streaming replication configured across node1 (writable primary), node2, node3 (standbys)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"pg_basebackup completed successfully from node1 to node2/node3 (cmd-c335de4356274c8b, cmd-e457ecc19fc54a4d). pg_stat_replication on node1 shows both node2 and node3 in 'streaming' state (cmd-c71a530eeca442ce). pg_is_in_recovery=t on both standbys (cmd-3fb8f10cae8246b6, cmd-652f6e1ed247498a) and pg_is_in_recovery=f on node1 (cmd-a90da5cd587e44b6), confirming node1 is the writable primary.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c335de4356274c8b\",\"cmd-e457ecc19fc54a4d\",\"cmd-c71a530eeca442ce\",\"cmd-3fb8f10cae8246b6\",\"cmd-652f6e1ed247498a\",\"cmd-a90da5cd587e44b6\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2-tls-ca\",\"requirement\":\"Replication traffic carried over TLS using a certificate authority created for this cluster\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A dedicated CA (ca.key/ca.crt, CN=pg-cluster-ca) was generated on node1 (cmd-7694f4e97087465d). Per-node server certs and a replicator client cert were issued from that CA (cmd-e7f7e2deb8cc4cd0, cmd-cbe01f2ee20242f6) and distributed/installed into each node's data directory (cmd-4fa38f61a6d746c9, cmd-c289c16ca9d94df7). SSL was enabled (SHOW ssl = on, cmd-ee965c30a7cd4012) and pg_stat_ssl confirms ssl=t on both live replication connections (cmd-b2794c18eb684131).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7694f4e97087465d\",\"cmd-e7f7e2deb8cc4cd0\",\"cmd-cbe01f2ee20242f6\",\"cmd-ee965c30a7cd4012\",\"cmd-b2794c18eb684131\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3-ca-only-peers\",\"requirement\":\"Only peers presenting a certificate issued by the cluster CA are accepted for replication connections\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"pg_hba.conf on node1 restricts replication access to 'hostssl replication replicator <ip>/32 cert clientcert=1' for the three cluster IPs, with no other rule matching replication traffic (cmd-6e62975b3c4a4072). A connection attempt using a self-signed, non-CA client cert with CN=replicator was rejected at the TLS handshake with 'SSL error: tlsv1 alert unknown ca' (cmd-02973bf4e62f4054), directly demonstrating enforcement, not just configuration.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-6e62975b3c4a4072\",\"cmd-bde08ade237e4911\",\"cmd-02973bf4e62f4054\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4-data-correctness\",\"requirement\":\"End-to-end replicated data correctness (writes on primary appear on standbys)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A row inserted on node1 (cmd-60b6781ec4664560) was observed on node2 and node3 shortly after (cmd-8fc36595ce3f4f06, cmd-f55d1d8fa7c94dd6), confirming functioning streaming replication beyond just connection status.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-60b6781ec4664560\",\"cmd-8fc36595ce3f4f06\",\"cmd-f55d1d8fa7c94dd6\"]},{\"id\":\"req-5-node-restart-evidence\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on every managed node with pre/post boot identity, restart ack, and recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For all three nodes: baseline boot_id and healthy state captured (cmd-a90da5cd587e44b6, cmd-8b9bf29d9a244aa5, cmd-9d7f6192306b4bb5), reboot acknowledgement returned before disconnect (cmd-0bd8095953914c8f, cmd-2d15bb10b46b46a5, cmd-786bc413b79e402c), a different post-restart boot_id with uptime reset to 0 was observed after each (cmd-33da49dc138147cf, cmd-0cb0483d63c249cd, cmd-a6e0c1ea2cb8463f), and recovered service/data/replication state was directly confirmed on each node afterward (cmd-f060e25430a942c6, cmd-abf9385759bc42ea, cmd-04a580e6e96943d0, cmd-62ac17b61ffd49d1, cmd-711d72c872f740a4, cmd-ff79317f59b04571), including a post-restart primary write propagating to both standbys. The fixed after-executor lifecycle snapshot boot identities match the executor-observed post-restart boot_ids for all three nodes, corroborating the transition.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a90da5cd587e44b6\",\"cmd-8b9bf29d9a244aa5\",\"cmd-9d7f6192306b4bb5\",\"cmd-0bd8095953914c8f\",\"cmd-2d15bb10b46b46a5\",\"cmd-786bc413b79e402c\",\"cmd-33da49dc138147cf\",\"cmd-0cb0483d63c249cd\",\"cmd-a6e0c1ea2cb8463f\",\"cmd-f060e25430a942c6\",\"cmd-abf9385759bc42ea\",\"cmd-04a580e6e96943d0\",\"cmd-62ac17b61ffd49d1\",\"cmd-711d72c872f740a4\",\"cmd-ff79317f59b04571\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.85,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.6,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands were purposeful (installs, config edits, cert issuance/deployment, basebackup, restarts) and directly tied to the task. Two notable issues: (1) The cluster CA private key (ca.key) and per-node/replicator private keys generated in /tmp/pgca on node1 (cmd-7694f4e97087465d, cmd-e7f7e2deb8cc4cd0, cmd-cbe01f2ee20242f6) were left in place with group/other-readable permissions (observed as -rw-rw-r-- in cmd-7694f4e97087465d's directory listing) and never cleaned up or permission-restricted, and equivalent copies of node/replicator private keys were left under /tmp on node2 and node3 (cmd-b9eab7fc31d54d0b, cmd-4fa38f61a6d746c9, cmd-c289c16ca9d94df7) — this is unremoved, security-relevant residue (a locally-readable copy of cluster-signing key material) rather than a bounded reverted action. (2) The rogue/self-signed test certificate used to validate CA enforcement was properly cleaned up afterward (cmd-11a4f648a5024503, rm -f /tmp/rogue.key /tmp/rogue.crt) — a well-bounded, fully reverted diagnostic action, not penalized. Several early failed attempts (permission errors copying certs, sed syntax errors, wal_level typo, recovery.conf home-dir permission errors) were read/no-op failures immediately corrected, not unwanted mutations.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7694f4e97087465d\",\"cmd-e7f7e2deb8cc4cd0\",\"cmd-cbe01f2ee20242f6\",\"cmd-b9eab7fc31d54d0b\",\"cmd-4fa38f61a6d746c9\",\"cmd-c289c16ca9d94df7\",\"cmd-11a4f648a5024503\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task instruction are satisfied with direct evidence: TLS-encrypted streaming replication from node1 (writable primary) to node2/node3, backed by a purpose-created cluster CA, with pg_hba.conf restricted to CA-issued client certificates and this restriction actively demonstrated by
