 in /tmp on all three nodes with weak (group/other-readable) permissions and never cleaned up, which is a security-relevant residue independent of task functionality.\",\"limitations\":[\"Verification relies entirely on executor-reported command transcripts (psql output, openssl/pg_hba output); no independent tool access was available to re-verify certificate chains, file permissions system-wide, or current pg_hba.conf/postgresql.conf contents.\",\"The exact live file permissions of the leftover /tmp key material on node2/node3 were not explicitly re-listed after copying (only inferred from analogous listings on node1 and standard scp/cp behavior), so the precise exposure severity of that residue is not fully confirmed.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1-topology","requirement":"PostgreSQL streaming replication configured across node1 (writable primary), node2, node3 (standbys)","status":"satisfied","summary":"pg_basebackup completed successfully from node1 to node2/node3 (cmd-c335de4356274c8b, cmd-e457ecc19fc54a4d). pg_stat_replication on node1 shows both node2 and node3 in 'streaming' state (cmd-c71a530eeca442ce). pg_is_in_recovery=t on both standbys (cmd-3fb8f10cae8246b6, cmd-652f6e1ed247498a) and pg_is_in_recovery=f on node1 (cmd-a90da5cd587e44b6), confirming node1 is the writable primary.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c335de4356274c8b","cmd-e457ecc19fc54a4d","cmd-c71a530eeca442ce","cmd-3fb8f10cae8246b6","cmd-652f6e1ed247498a","cmd-a90da5cd587e44b6"]},{"id":"req-2-tls-ca","requirement":"Replication traffic carried over TLS using a certificate authority created for this cluster","status":"satisfied","summary":"A dedicated CA (ca.key/ca.crt, CN=pg-cluster-ca) was generated on node1 (cmd-7694f4e97087465d). Per-node server certs and a replicator client cert were issued from that CA (cmd-e7f7e2deb8cc4cd0, cmd-cbe01f2ee20242f6) and distributed/installed into each node's data directory (cmd-4fa38f61a6d746c9, cmd-c289c16ca9d94df7). SSL was enabled (SHOW ssl 